Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and how they will probably be used  
(event‑level information is stored in the daily tables):

• `event_name`            : filter to `session_start` events (one row per GA4 session).  
• `event_date`            : keep the events that belong to December 2020 (`event_date` BETWEEN '20201201' AND '20201231').  
• `event_params`          : extract the parameters that define a session  
  – `'ga_session_id'`     : numeric session identifier  
  – `'source'` / `'medium'` / `'campaign'` : build traffic‑channel rules  
• `user_pseudo_id`        : combine with the session id to de‑duplicate sessions.  
• `traffic_source.source` / `traffic_source.medium` : user‑level fallback when the same keys are missing in `event_params`.

Typical conditions that can be applied  
```
WHERE event_name = 'session_start'
AND  event_date BETWEEN '20201201' AND '20201231'
```
Inside a SELECT list one can bring any parameter with
```
( SELECT ep.value.string_value
  FROM   UNNEST(event_params) AS ep
  WHERE  ep.key = 'source' )   AS source
```
(or change `'source'` to any other key).

Below are ten exploratory queries (simple → complex).  
Every query is limited to 20 rows so you can quickly inspect the data that drive the final answer.

```sql
-- 1) Description: Distinct list of event names on 1 Dec 2020
SELECT DISTINCT `event_name`
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_20201201`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Description: See all event‑param keys that appear in session_start events on 1 Dec 2020
SELECT DISTINCT ep.key
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_20201201`,
       UNNEST(event_params) AS ep
WHERE  event_name = 'session_start'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Description: Get a sample of session_start rows with the numeric GA session id
SELECT
  user_pseudo_id,
  (SELECT ep.value.int_value FROM UNNEST(event_params) ep WHERE ep.key = 'ga_session_id') AS ga_session_id
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_20201203`
WHERE  event_name = 'session_start'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
